nagement and Entrepreneurial Studies Head Coach, Men’s Soccer Head Coach, eSports Prelicensure Nursing Program, Parsippany NJ – Clinical Adjunct Faculty Associate Professor – PsyD Counseling Psychology Program Campus Security: Part-time Security Officer Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Management/Entrepreneurial Studies Faculty Inter-Campus Shuttle Bus Drivers Inter-Campus Shuttle Bus Drivers Half-Time Instructor, Prelicensure Nursing IT Help Desk Support Technician – Temporary Director of Institutional Assessment and Accreditation Full-time Faculty, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Evening and Weekend Circulation Supervisor Research and Instruction Librarian Faculty Adjunct – Mathematics Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Adjunct Faculty, English Conference and Event Services Directions & Maps On Campus Tours History & Tradition Office of the President Senior Administrative Officers Alumni REED Autism Services Partnership Felician University, the Franciscan University of New Jersey is seeking a dynamic, enthusiastic, detailed-oriented and student-focused financial support professional to serve as Associate Director of Student Financial Service Operations. Reporting to the Director of Financial Aid, the Associate Director provides management, administration, and strategic oversight of federal, state, and institutional financial aid programs, as well as student accounts, at Felician University. S/he co-manages system setup, staff training, systems integration, troubleshooting, and reporting within the University’s information systems, with a focus on continuous innovation and the enhancement of student financial services processes. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. We offer a choice of medical, dental, vision, and life insurance benefits, as well as a retirement plan (403B), tuition remission, and generous time off benefits. Required Education: Bachelor’s degree, BA/BS, required. Qualifications: 3–5 years of progressively responsible administrative experience in higher education financial aid administration, proven leadership and management skills, with the ability to set goals and objectives to effectively oversee Student Financial Services operations and systems, strong program analysis and evaluation skills, with the ability to provide insightful findings and actionable recommendations, demonstrated functional and technical knowledge required to perform at a high level in the role, experience with computerized student financial services systems; Colleague experience preferred. Excellent analytical, creative thinking, and problem-solving skills, strong interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively with diverse populations, demonstrating professionalism, flexibility, sensitivity, and a collaborative spirit, proven ability to work independently while managing multiple priorities and deadlines; must be detail-oriented and adaptable to changing needs, outstanding written and verbal communication skills, competency in delivering presentations to both small and large groups, strong organizational and time-management skills, commitment to and ability to support the Felician Franciscan mission and core values of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, current curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information for (two) 2 professional references electronically to: Director or via USPS to: Ms. Kathy Prieto, Director Student Financial Services Felician University 262 South Main Street Lodi, New Jersey 07644 Salary: $51,500 – $66,500 About Felici