urance benefits, as well as a retirement plan (403B), tuition remission, and generous time off benefits. Required Education: Master of Science in Nursing required, doctoral degree preferred. Faculty teaching in the graduate program must have an earned doctoral degree or currently enrolled in doctoral program Qualifications: Licensure in New Jersey as a Registered Nurse. Graduate Faculty must have current national certification and NJ Board of Nursing licensure as a Family Nurse Practitioner. 2+ years’ practical experience in the area of specialization. Proven knowledge and expertise in clinical nursing education. Previous teaching experience, preferably in an institution of higher education. Superior written and verbal communications skills. Ability to engage with students of diverse backgrounds and experiences. Willingness and ability to support and promote the Felician Franciscan mission and values of the University. To Apply: Send CV and three (3) professional references to Associate Dean or via USPS to: Ms. Erin Vitale, Associate Dean School of Nursing Felician University 262 South Main Street Lodi, New Jersey 07644 Salary: $83,000 to $88,100 About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Assistant Professor, Cybersecurity and Computer Sciences Assistant Professor, Management and Entrepreneurial Studies Assistant Professor, Marketing Assistant