ntrepreneurial Studies Head Coach, Men’s Soccer Head Coach, eSports Prelicensure Nursing Program, Parsippany NJ – Clinical Adjunct Faculty Associate Professor – PsyD Counseling Psychology Program Campus Security: Part-time Security Officer Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Management/Entrepreneurial Studies Faculty Inter-Campus Shuttle Bus Drivers Inter-Campus Shuttle Bus Drivers Half-Time Instructor, Prelicensure Nursing IT Help Desk Support Technician – Temporary Director of Institutional Assessment and Accreditation Full-time Faculty, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Evening and Weekend Circulation Supervisor Research and Instruction Librarian Faculty Adjunct – Mathematics Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Adjunct Faculty, English Conference and Event Services Directions & Maps On Campus Tours History & Tradition Office of the President Senior Administrative Officers Alumni REED Autism Services Partnership Felician University is presently seeking an innovative, highly motivated, flexible and goal-oriented professional to serve as Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services.  Reporting to the Director of Transfer and Adult Enrollment, the Assistant Director is responsible for collaborating in the planning and implementation of recruitment strategies and activities designed to increase enrollment of transfer students in conjunction with the University’s partnership with Bergen Community College.  S/he serves as the admissions officer and initial financial aid and academic advisor to students transferring from Berger Community College in traditional undergraduate or adult undergraduate programs. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. We offer a choice of medical, dental, vision, and life insurance benefits, as well as a retirement plan (403B), tuition remission, and generous time off benefits. Required Education: BA/BS degree required; Master’s degree in related field preferred Qualifications: 2-3 years’ in higher education or enrollment/admissions/study abroad advising experience; superior written and verbal communication skills; demonstrated problem-solving skills; well-developed presentation skills; well-developed organizational and time-management skills; highly advanced interpersonal skills, sensitivity to and ability to engage effectively with and direct a culturally and religiously diverse student population; demonstrated ability to work autonomously with multiple priorities and deadlines; superior advising and counseling skills, with a comprehensive knowledge of academic programs; availability and willingness to work evenings and weekends as needed; demonstrated ability to exercise sound judgement when interacting with students, staff, faculty and other internal and external stakeholders;  knowledge of computer databases and information systems; familiarity with social networking venues; willingness and ability to support and promote the Felician Franciscan mission and values of the University. Experience with Ellucian/Colleague, CRM preferred; willingness and ability to travel and recruit in areas outside of assigned geographical area as needed; willingness and ability to support and promote he Felician Franciscan mission and core values of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume and 2 professional references electronically to: Director or via USPS to: Ms. Brianna Grausso, Director Transfer and Adult Enrollment 1 Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 Salary: Commensurate with experience About Felician University Accreditations Pu