      "title": "Program Analyst – Information Systems",
      "description": "Program Analyst - Information Systems - Felician University of New Jersey Skip Navigation MENU MENU News Events My Felician Alumni Giving Menu About About Felician University The University operates on two campuses in Lodi and Rutherford, New Jersey. The University is one of the institutions of higher learning conducted by the Felician Sisters in the United States. Founded by the Felician Sisters of Lodi, New Jersey, it began as Immaculate Conception Normal School with the first summer session commencing on July 5, 1923. History & Tradition Institutional Research Office of the President Senior Administrative Officers Board of Trustees Members Fast Facts Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Facilities and Resources Faculty and Staff Directory On Campus Tours Virtual Tour Directions & Maps Academics Academics at Felician University Felician University has four schools and an institute for you to explore a range of undergraduate, pre-professional, certificate, and graduate programs. Search through the program offerings and find the program that is right for you in the School of Arts and Sciences, School of Business and Information Sciences, Education, Nursing, or the Institute for Information Sciences. School of Arts & Sciences School of Education School of Business and Information Sciences School of Nursing The Felician Advantage Lenke Family Center for Innovation Center for Career & Academic Success Center for Academic Technology Honors Program STEM Office of the Registrar Catalogs Institutional Review Board Summer Programs Academic Events Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid at Felician University Inspiring courses that make you think, dedicated faculty who will push you further than you imagined, and hands-on experiences that will shape your career and future. No SAT/ACT Required Affordability Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Adult Undergraduate Admissions Transfer Admissions Our Admissions Representatives High School Guidance Counselor Portal Accepted Students International Students Veterans Services Student Financial Services Make Application Payment Parents Virtual and On Campus Tours Become a Corporate Partner Virtual Appointments Admission Events Campus Life Campus Life at Felician University Our goal is to provide our students with a quality out of class experience that supports and amplifies the teaching and learning process which is the heart of our University. Students may choose from a wide range of opportunities which are designed to help them develop their leadership abilities and to have an enjoyable collegiate experience with great memories that will never end. Office of Student Affairs Dining Services Student Handbook Technology Services Students with Disabilities Residence Life The Center for Student Development and Engagement Campus Safety Counseling and Wellness Services Title IX Campus Ministry University Library University Bookstore Emergency Telephone Numbers Parents Bus & Shuttle Schedules Athletics GET INFO VISIT APPLY News Events My Felician Alumni Giving About About Felician University The University operates on two campuses in Lodi and Rutherford, New Jersey. The University is one of the institutions of higher learning conducted by the Felician Sisters in the United States. Founded by the Felician Sisters of Lodi, New Jersey, it began as Immaculate Conception Normal School with the first summer session commencing on July 5, 1923. History & Tradition Institutional Research Office of the President Senior Administrative Officers Board of Trustees Members Fast Facts Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Facilities and Resources Faculty and Staff Directory On Campus Tours Virtual Tour Directions & Maps Academics Academics at Felician University Felician University has four schools and an institute for you to explore a range of undergraduate, pre-professional, certificate, and graduate programs. Search through the program offerings and find the program that is right for you in the School of Arts and Sciences, School of Business and Information Sciences, Education, Nursing, or the Institute for Information Sciences. School of Arts & Sciences School of Education School of Business and Information Sciences School of Nursing The Felician Advantage Lenke Family Center for Innovation Center for Career & Academic Success Center for Academic Technology Honors Program STEM Office of the Registrar Catalogs Institutional Review Board Summer Programs Academic Events Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid at Felician University Inspiring courses that make you think, dedicated faculty who will push you further than you imagined, and hands-on experiences that will shape your career and future. No SAT/ACT Required Affordability Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Adult Undergraduate Admissions Transfer Admissions Our Admissions Representatives High School Guidance Counselor Portal Accepted Students International Students Veterans Services Student Financial Services Make Application Payment Parents Virtual and On Campus Tours Become a Corporate Partner Virtual Appointments Admission Events Campus Life Campus Life at Felician University Our goal is to provide our students with a quality out of class experience that supports and amplifies the teaching and learning process which is the heart of our University. Students may choose from a wide range of opportunities which are designed to help them develop their leadership abilities and to have an enjoyable collegiate experience with great memories that will never end. Office of Student Affairs Dining Services Student Handbook Technology Services Students with Disabilities Residence Life The Center for Student Development and Engagement Campus Safety Counseling and Wellness Services Title IX Campus Ministry University Library University Bookstore Emergency Telephone Numbers Parents Bus & Shuttle Schedules Athletics GET INFO VISIT APPLY Home \\ About Felician University \\ Careers at Felician Program Analyst – Information Systems IN THIS SECTION About Felician University Summer Sports and Gaming Camps Board of Trustees Members Institutional Assessment Accreditations Middle States Self-Study Process Strategic Plan Fast Facts Careers at Felician Associate Director of Student Financial Services Operations Full-time Faculty – School of Nursing Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Program Analyst – Information Systems Faculty Adjunct – Graduate Nursing Assistant/Associate Professor, Mathematics Part-time Assistant Coach, Men’s Wrestling Associate Director of Student Accounts Clinical Adjunct Faculty, School of Nursing, Traditional ABSN, Rutherfod NJ Assistant Professor, Prelicensure Nursing Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Part-Time ESL Instructors  July 15-August 5, 2026 Faculty Adjuncts, Philosophy Security Officers Faculty Adjuncts, School of Business and Information Sciences Instructor, School of Nursing Faculty Adjunct, Communications Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Academic Success Coach JV Men’s Soccer Coach and Athletics Coordinator Full Time Faculty, Mathematics Assistant Professor, Cybersecurity and Computer Sciences Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Associate Director for Academic Operations Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Clinical Adjunct Faculty, Hybrid ABSN, Parsippany, School of Nursing Associate Director of Housing Operations Associate Director of Transfer Student Success Part-Time Professional Science Tutor Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Building and Grounds Assistant Attitude Against Violence Project Coordinator Assistant/Associate Professor, Chemistry Head Coach, Women’s Acrobatics and Tumbling Assistant Professor, Marketing Assessment Data Coordinator Engagement and Philanthropy Officer Director of Internships and Assessment, School of Education Assistant Sports Information Director and Intramurals Coordinator Assistant Professor, Management and Entrepreneurial Studies Head Coach, Men’s Soccer Head Coach, eSports Prelicensure Nursing Program, Parsippany NJ – Clinical Adjunct Faculty Associate Professor – PsyD Counseling Psychology Program Campus Security: Part-time Security Officer Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Management/Entrepreneurial Studies Faculty Inter-Campus Shuttle Bus Drivers Inter-Campus Shuttle Bus Drivers Half-Time Instructor, Prelicensure Nursing IT Help Desk Support Technician – Temporary Director of Institutional Assessment and Accreditation Full-time Faculty, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Evening and Weekend Circulation Supervisor Research and Instruction Librarian Faculty Adjunct – Mathematics Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Adjunct Faculty, English Conference and Event Services Directions & Maps On Campus Tours History & Tradition Office of the President Senior Administrative Officers Alumni REED Autism Services Partnership Program Analyst – Information Systems Felician University is presently seeking a dynamic, detailed and service-oriented information technology specialist to serve as Program Analyst for the Office of Information Systems.  Reporting to the Associate Director of Information Systems, the Program Analyst supports the senior staff with task related to design, development, integration, and maintenance software and reporting. This role works closely with the operation departments to understand business needs, translate requirements into solutions and ensure the reliability and effectiveness of enterprise systems such as the student information systems (SIS), ERP platforms, and related applications, that support student, financial, and academic operations. This is an in-person, on-campus position. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. We offer a choice of medical, dental, vision, and life insurance benefits, as well as a retirement plan (403B), tuition remission, and generous time off benefits. Required Education: BS in Information Systems/Technology, Computer Science or equivalent required; Master’s degree preferred. Qualifications: Experience working in a Higher Education environment. Functional knowledge in Ellucian Colleague, MS SQL/Server, and MS T-SQL. Preferred experience with Informer, Java/JavaScript, MS Office, and other methods as needed to create reports for campus end users. Knowledge of APIs for assistance in implementation of new software and solutions. Requirements gathering and business analysis skills with an understanding of higher-education administrative processes. Data governance and security awareness High degree of personal motivation, self-management, and detail orientation. Diverse organizational, analytical, and technical skills in report writing, systems integration, development, and maintenance. Ability to translate technical concepts for non-technical users. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills with an analytical and problem-solving mindset Ability to work both independently and collaboratively within and across departments. Well-developed critical thinking skills, ability to communicate both verbally and in writing with technical staff and customers across departments. Flexibility and willingness to work occasional evenings and weekends as needed. Willingness and ability to support and promote the Felician Franciscan mission and core values of the University. Salary Range $65,000 – $76,000 To Apply: Please email cover letter, three (3) professional references and CV/resume electronically to Associate Director or via USPS to: Ms. Cynthia Vincenti, Associate Director Information Systems Felician University 262 South Main Street Lodi, New Jersey 07644 About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Assistant Professor, Cybersecurity and Computer Sciences Assistant Professor, Management and Entrepreneurial Studies Assistant Professor, Marketing Assistant Professor, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Sports Information Director and Intramurals Coordinator Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant/Associate Professor, Mathematics Associate Director for Academic Operations Associate Director of Housing Operations Associate Director of Student Accounts Associate Director of Student Financial Services Operations Associate Director of Transfer Student Success Associate Professor – PsyD Counseling Psychology Program Attitude Against Violence Project Coordinator Building and Grounds Assistant Campus Security: Part-time Security Officer Clinical Adjunct Faculty, Hybrid ABSN, Parsippany, School of Nursing Clinical Adjunct Faculty, School of Nursing, Traditional ABSN, Rutherfod NJ Director of Institutional Assessment and Accreditation Director of Internships and Assessment, School of Education Engagement and Philanthropy Officer Evening and Weekend Circ