es Head Coach, Men’s Soccer Head Coach, eSports Prelicensure Nursing Program, Parsippany NJ – Clinical Adjunct Faculty Associate Professor – PsyD Counseling Psychology Program Campus Security: Part-time Security Officer Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Management/Entrepreneurial Studies Faculty Inter-Campus Shuttle Bus Drivers Inter-Campus Shuttle Bus Drivers Half-Time Instructor, Prelicensure Nursing IT Help Desk Support Technician – Temporary Director of Institutional Assessment and Accreditation Full-time Faculty, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Evening and Weekend Circulation Supervisor Research and Instruction Librarian Faculty Adjunct – Mathematics Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Adjunct Faculty, English Conference and Event Services Directions & Maps On Campus Tours History & Tradition Office of the President Senior Administrative Officers Alumni REED Autism Services Partnership Felician University, the Franciscan University of New Jersey, seeks an academically qualified specialist to serve as Assistant/Associate Professor of Mathematics in the School of Arts and Sciences for the 2025-2026 academic year. Candidates should have experience teaching in a traditional and online environment and must be willing to pursue Felician online certification.  S/he must possess comprehensive mathematical expertise to teach across the complete spectrum of undergraduate mathematics courses, from developmental and foundational courses through advanced upper-level offerings required for the bachelor’s degree in mathematics. S/he will serve students at all levels of mathematical preparation utilizing exceptional communication skills to make complex mathematical concepts accessible and engaging for diverse learners. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. We offer a  choice of medical, dental, vision, and life insurance benefits, as well as a retirement plan (403B), tuition remission, and generous time off benefits. Position Type: Full-time, 10-months, Exempt Department: Mathematics, School of Arts and Sciences Required Education: Earned doctoral degree in Mathematics or related field such as Mathematics Education or Applied Mathematics Qualifications: Demonstrated expertise across the full spectrum of undergraduate mathematics curriculum from developmental through advanced coursework. Minimum of two years teaching experience in mathematics at the college level. Strong verbal and written communication skills with proven ability to explain complex mathematical concepts clearly and effectively. Demonstrated skill in working with students of diverse academic backgrounds and learning styles. Proficiency with mathematical software, learning management systems, and educational technology tools. Ability to adapt teaching methods to accommodate different learning preferences and academic preparation levels. Strong organizational and time management skills. Commitment to fostering an inclusive and supportive learning environment for all students. Ability and willingness to support and promote the Felician Franciscan core values and mission of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, current curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information for two professional references electronically to the Associate Dean or via USPS to: Dr. Gaby Fahmy, Associate Dean School of Arts and Sciences Felician University 262 South Main Street Lodi, New Jersey 07644 About Felician University Summer Sports and Gaming Camps Board of Trustees Members Institutional Assessment Accreditations Middle