ll as a retirement plan (403B), tuition remission, and generous time off benefits. Required Education: Masters of Science in Nursing required, doctoral degree preferred.  Faculty teaching in the graduate program must have an earned doctoral degree or currently enrolled in doctoral program Qualifications: Licensure in New Jersey as a Registered Nurse.  Graduate Faculty must have current national certification and NJ Board of Nursing licensure as a Family Nurse Practitioner. 2+ years’ practical experience in the area of specialization. Comprehensive knowledge of and experience in clinical nursing education. Previous teaching experience, preferably in an institution of higher education. Superior written and verbal communications skills. Ability to engage with students of diverse backgrounds and experiences. Willingness and ability to support and promote the Felician Franciscan mission and values of the University. To Apply: Send CV and three (3) professional references to Interim Dean or via USPS to: Dr. Patricia Munno, Interim Dean School of Nursing Felician University 262 South Main Street Lodi, New Jersey 07644 Salary Range: $83,000 – $88,100, commensurate with rank, experience and certifications About Felician University Summer Sports and Gaming Camps Board of Trustees Members Institutional Assessment Accreditations Middle States Self-Study Process Strategic Plan Fast Facts Careers at Felician Associate Director of Student Financial Services Operations Full-time Faculty – School of Nursing Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Program Analyst – Information Systems Faculty Adjunct – Graduate Nursing Assistant/Associate Professor, Mathematics Part-time Assistant Coach, Men’s Wrestling Associate Director of Student Accounts Clinical Adjunct Faculty, School of Nursing, Traditional ABSN, Rutherfod NJ Assistant Professor, Prelicensure Nursing Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Part-Time ESL Instructors  July 15-August 5, 2026 Faculty Adjuncts, Philosoph