ccepted Students International Students Veterans Services Student Financial Services Make Application Payment Parents Virtual and On Campus Tours Become a Corporate Partner Virtual Appointments Admission Events Campus Life Campus Life at Felician University Our goal is to provide our students with a quality out of class experience that supports and amplifies the teaching and learning process which is the heart of our University. Students may choose from a wide range of opportunities which are designed to help them develop their leadership abilities and to have an enjoyable collegiate experience with great memories that will never end. Office of Student Affairs Dining Services Student Handbook Technology Services Students with Disabilities Residence Life The Center for Student Development and Engagement Campus Safety Counseling and Wellness Services Title IX Campus Ministry University Library University Bookstore Emergency Telephone Numbers Parents Bus & Shuttle Schedules Athletics GET INFO VISIT APPLY News Events My Felician Alumni Giving About About Felician University The University operates on two campuses in Lodi and Rutherford, New Jersey. The University is one of the institutions of higher learning conducted by the Felician Sisters in the United States. Founded by the Felician Sisters of Lodi, New Jersey, it began as Immaculate Conception Normal School with the first summer session commencing on July 5, 1923. History & Tradition Institutional Research Office of the President Senior Administrative Officers Board of Trustees Members Fast Facts Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Facilities and Resources Faculty and Staff Directory On Campus Tours Virtual Tour Directions & Maps Academics Academics at Felician University Felician University has four schools and an institute for you to explore a range of undergraduate, pre-professional, certificate, and graduate programs. Search through the program offerings and find the program that is right for you in the School of Arts and Sciences, School of Business and Information Sciences, Education, Nursing, or the Institute for Information Sciences. School of Arts & Sciences School of Education School of Business and Information Sciences School of Nursing The Felician Advantage Lenke Family Center for Innovation Center for Career & Academic Success Center for Academic Technology Honors Program STEM Office of the Registrar Catalogs Institutional Review Board Summer Programs Academic Events Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid at Felician University Inspiring courses that make you think, dedicated faculty who will push you further than you imagined, and hands-on experiences that will shape your career and future. No SAT/ACT Required Affordability Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Adult Undergraduate Admissions Transfer Admissions Our Admissions Representatives High School Guidance Counselor Portal Accepted Students International Students Veterans Services Student Financial Services Make Application Payment Parents Virtual and On Campus Tours Become a Corporate Partner Virtual Appointments Admission Events Campus Life Campus Life at Felician University Our goal is to provide our students with a quality out of class experience that supports and amplifies the teaching and learning process which is the heart of our University. Students may choose from a wide range of opportunities which are designed to help them develop their leadership abilities and to have an enjoyable collegiate experience with great memories that will never end. Office of Student Affairs Dining Services Student Handbook Technology Services Students with Disabilities Residence Life The Center for Student Development and Engagement Campus Safety Counseling and Wellness Services Title IX Campus Ministry University Library University Bookstore Emergency Telephone Numbers Parents Bus & Shuttle Schedules Athletics GET INFO VISIT APPLY Home \\ About Felician University \\ Careers at Felician Security Officers Felician University is presently seeking dedicated and observant Campus Security officers to help protect our campus community, facilities and assets.  The Security Officer engages in a wide variety of activities, including but not limited to: conducting active patrols of campus grounds, buildings, parking areas and walkways to ensure safety and security; monitoring surveillance systems and responding promptly to alarms or suspicious activity; enforcing campus policies, rules and regulations in a fair and respectful manner; providing assistance during emergencies, including medical incidents, evacuations, and severe weather events; preparing accurate incident and activity reports; offering directions, information and assistance to students, staff and visitors. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. We offer a  choice of medical, dental, vision, and life insurance benefits, as well as a retirement plan (403B), tuition remission, and generous time off benefits for full-time employees, and sick time benefits for part-time employees. P osition Type: A variety part-time and full-time shifts available, weekdays, nights and weekends Department: Campus Safety and Security Date Posted: December 19, 2025 Required Education: High school diploma or equivalent required, Associate’s or Bachelor’s degree in Criminal justice or related field a plus Essential Qualifications: Ability and willingness to act to ensure the safety and security of the property, students, staff, faculty and visitors to the University in accordance with University policy, prior security experience in a college/university setting preferred;  strong communication and interpersonal skills; ability to remain calm and make sound decisions under pressure; current Security Officer Registration Act (SORA) certification or willingness and ability to attain such upon position confirmation prior to beginning employment; ability to fulfill the physical requirements of the position, including heavy lifting within manageable and safe parameters (25-50 pounds), ability to stand, walk, stoop, climb, and bend, and  ability to work outdoors in all seasons as needed; proven ability to work with a diverse population, experience working with teenagers and young adults preferred; certification in First Aid, CPR, and/or AED a plus; willingness and ability to model, support and promote the Felician Franciscan mission and values of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume, and 2 references electronically to the Director or via USPS to: Mr. Heath James Director, Campus Safety and Security 1 Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 Salary: $17.50/hour About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Assistant Professor, Cybersecurity and Computer Sciences Assistant Professor, Management and Entrepreneurial Studies Assistant Professor, Marketing Assistant Professor, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Sports Information Director and Intramurals Coordinator Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant/Associate Professor, Mathematics Associate Director for Academic Operations Associate Director of Housing Operations Associate Director of Student Accounts Associate Director of Student Financial Services Operations Associate Director of Transfer Student Success Associate Professor – PsyD Counseling Psychology Program Attitude Against Violence Project Coordinator Building and Grounds Assistant Campus Security: Part-time Security Officer Clinical Adjunct Faculty, Hybrid ABSN, Parsippany, School of Nursing Clinical Adjunct Faculty, School of Nursing, Traditional ABSN, Rutherfod NJ Director of Institutional Assessment and Accreditation Director of Internships and Assessment, School of Education Engagement and Philanthropy Officer Evening and Weekend Circulation Supervisor Faculty Adjunct – Mathematics Faculty Adjunct – Graduate Nursing Faculty Adjunct, Communications Faculty Adjuncts, Philosophy Faculty Adjuncts, School of Business and Information Sciences Full Time Faculty, Mathematics Full-time Faculty – School of Nursing Full-time Faculty, Prelicensure Nursing Half-Time Instructor, Prelicensure Nursing Head Coach, eSports Head Coach, Men’s Soccer Head Coach, Women’s Acrobatics and Tumbling Instructor, School of Nursing Inter-Campus Shuttle Bus Drivers Inter-Campus Shuttle Bus Drivers IT Help Desk Support Technician – Temporary JV Men’s Soccer Coach and Athletics Coordinator Management/Entrepreneurial Studies Faculty Part-time Assistant Coach, Men’s Wrestling Part-Time ESL Instructors  July 15-August 5, 2026 Part-Time Professional Science Tutor Prelicensure Nursing Program, Parsippany NJ – Clinical Adjunct Faculty Program Analyst – Information Systems Research and Instruction Librarian Security Officers Conference and Event Services Directions & Maps Fast Facts History & Tradition Felician Franciscan Ministry Institutional Assessment Institutional Assessment Plan Mission, Values, and Objectives Middle States Self-Study Process Co-Chairs for Working Groups Communication Plan Institutional Priorities Intended Outcomes Self-Study Design Strategic Plan 2025-2028 Timetable for Middle States Updates Working Group Charges Office of the President History of the Felician Presidency Inaugural Speech of Dr. Anne Prisco Message From the President On Campus Tours REED Autism Services Partnership Senior Administrative Officers Strategic Plan Summer Sports and Gaming Camps CONTACT INFORMATION Felician University One Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 Phone: 201.559.6000 Phone: 201.355.1465 Contact Us | Directions & Maps | Campus Emergency Information | Request Information | Students Right to Know and Achievement | Privacy policy | Anti-Discrimination Policy | Accessibility TOP Felician University - One Felician Way, Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 201.559.6000 / 201.355.1465 Felician University uses cookies to provide necessary website functionality, improve your experience and analyze our traffic. By using our website, you agree to our Privacy Policy and our cookies usage. Accept Close GDPR Cookie Settings Privacy Overview Strictly Necessary Cookies Powered by GDPR Cookie Compliance Privacy Overview This website uses cookies so that we can provide you with the best user experience possible. Cookie information is stored in your browser and performs functions such as recognising you when you return to our website and helping our team to understand which sections of the website you find most interesting and useful. Strictly Necessary Cookies Strictly Necessary Cookie should be enabled at all times so that we can save your preferences for cookie settings. Enable or Disable Cookies Enabled Disabled Enable All Save Settings"
