sity \\ Careers at Felician Faculty Adjuncts, School of Business and Information Sciences Felician University is offering a variety of exciting opportunities for passionate and experienced educators to join our growing team of Adjunct Faculty in the School of Business and Information Sciences for the 2024-2025 academic year. Our faculty adjuncts help to shape the minds of tomorrow’s leaders and support and promote the next generation of tech-savvy professionals through mentoring students in dynamic Master’s-level courses grounded in real-world applications, delivering engaging instructions using best practices in higher education and areas of expertise, and collaborating with our dedicated full-time faculty to foster a supportive learning environment. Opportunities are available in three areas of academic studies: Computer Science Data Science Cyber Security We offer flexible opportunities to fit your schedule: Part-time positions teaching 1-2 courses per semester. Schedule variety, with daytime, evening, and online courses available to accommodate your preferences. A maximum of 3 days per week to ensure work-life balance. Essential Qualifications include: Master’s degree in Computer Science, Data Science, Cyber Security or a closely related field. Teaching experience, preferably at the graduate level. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to engage with a diverse student population. Passion for sharing knowledge. Demonstrated commitment to student success. Experience with BrightSpace LMS preferred. Ability and willingness to support and promote the Franciscan Felician core values and mission of the University. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. To apply, send your cover letter, current CV, and two (2) professional references electronically to S chool of Business and Information Sciences , or via USPS to: Dr. David Turi, Associate Dean School of Business and Information Sciences Felician University 1 Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey  07070 About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Assistant Professor, Cybersecurity and Computer Sciences Assistant Professor, Management and Entrepreneurial Studies Assistant Professor, Marketing Assistant Professor, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Sports Information Director and Intramurals Coordinator Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant/Associate Professor, Mathematics Associate Director for Academic Operations Associate Director of Housing Operations Associate Director of Student Accounts Associate Director of Student Financial Services Operations Associate Director of Transfer Student Success Associate Professor – PsyD Counseling Psychology Program Attitude Against Violence Project Coordinator Building and Grounds Assistant Campus Security: Part-time Security Officer Clinical Adjunct Faculty, Hybrid ABSN, Parsippany, School of Nursing Clinical Adjunct Faculty, School of Nursing, Traditional ABSN, Rutherfod NJ Director of Institutional Assessment and Accreditation Director of Internships and Ass