occer Head Coach, eSports Prelicensure Nursing Program, Parsippany NJ – Clinical Adjunct Faculty Associate Professor – PsyD Counseling Psychology Program Campus Security: Part-time Security Officer Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Management/Entrepreneurial Studies Faculty Inter-Campus Shuttle Bus Drivers Inter-Campus Shuttle Bus Drivers Half-Time Instructor, Prelicensure Nursing IT Help Desk Support Technician – Temporary Director of Institutional Assessment and Accreditation Full-time Faculty, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Evening and Weekend Circulation Supervisor Research and Instruction Librarian Faculty Adjunct – Mathematics Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Adjunct Faculty, English Conference and Event Services Directions & Maps On Campus Tours History & Tradition Office of the President Senior Administrative Officers Alumni REED Autism Services Partnership Felician University is presently offering an exciting opportunity for an energetic and goal-oriented individual with coaching experience in collegiate women’s soccer to serve as the part-time Assistant Coach for our dynamic women’s soccer team.  The Assistant Coach serves as a primary instructor for players, as well as assisting the Head Coach in the supervision all aspects of a NCAA national Collegiate Women’s Soccer program.  Reporting to the Director of Athletics, the Assistant Coach assists in the preparation and execution of individual and team practices, training and competition; making travel arrangements for away competitions; identifying and recruiting potential women’s basketball student-athletes, including email, phone and mail correspondence; monitoring players’ academic progress; complying with all aspects of the Felician University Coach’s manual. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. Required Education: Bachelor’s degree in related field required; may be waived for extensive practical experience in the field Qualifications: 2+ years’ successful soccer coaching experience; comprehensive knowledge of NCAA rules and regulations; ability to work well with a diverse group of student athletes; strong written and verbal communications skills; well-developed leadership skills; outstanding organizational and follow through skills; strong commitment to support and promote the Franciscan Felician values and function effectively within a Catholic University environment. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume and contact information for at least 3 professional references electronically to: Head Coach or via USPS to: Mr. Scott Maloney, Head Coach Felician University 1 Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 Salary: Commensurate with experience About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Assistant Professor, Cybersecurity and Computer Sciences Assistant Professor, Management and Entrepreneurial Studies Assistant Professor, Marketing Assistant Professor, Prelicensure Nursing Ass