eSports Prelicensure Nursing Program, Parsippany NJ – Clinical Adjunct Faculty Associate Professor – PsyD Counseling Psychology Program Campus Security: Part-time Security Officer Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Management/Entrepreneurial Studies Faculty Inter-Campus Shuttle Bus Drivers Inter-Campus Shuttle Bus Drivers Half-Time Instructor, Prelicensure Nursing IT Help Desk Support Technician – Temporary Director of Institutional Assessment and Accreditation Full-time Faculty, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Evening and Weekend Circulation Supervisor Research and Instruction Librarian Faculty Adjunct – Mathematics Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Adjunct Faculty, English Conference and Event Services Directions & Maps On Campus Tours History & Tradition Office of the President Senior Administrative Officers Alumni REED Autism Services Partnership Felician University, the Franciscan University of New Jersey seeking a Nursing professional to serve as a Nursing Success Coach for the upcoming Fall semester.  The Nursing Success Coach is responsible for developing and conducting retention and support activities for students identified as “at-risk of failing” in the Hybrid ABSN Nursing Program.  S/he provides direct academic support, mentoring and coordinated service delivery plan and connects students to needed resources with the primary purpose of improving course completion and graduation outcomes in the Hybrid ABSN Program. The positions are primarily remote and will require access to and familiarity with remote learning venues, i.e., Zoom, Microsoft teams. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. Position Type: Per diem, 12-month, Non-Exempt Department: School of Nursing Date Posted: Monday, August 21, 2023 Required Education: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution required, Master’s degree in Nursing preferred. Qualifications: Current NJ license in good standing as a Registered Nurse, NJ Registered Nurse license required throughout employment in the position; knowledge of student development and resources to promote student success; previous experience mentoring or precepting; demonstrated experience maintaining confidentiality (HIPPA and FERPA); strong working knowledge of Microsoft Office applications and online learning platforms such as Canvas LMS; ability, willingness and equipment required to utilize remote instructional venues, i.e., Zoom; strong organizational skills with the ability to work independently; availability and willingness to work a flexible schedule which includes evenings and weekends; ability to effectively track student participation and success rates; ability to communicate effectively with prospective and current students, staff faculty, administration, colleagues and community partners in large and small group settings; ability and willingness to support and promote the Felician Franciscan mission and core values of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume, and the names and contact information for (two) 2 professional references electronically to the Associate Dean or via USPS to: Ms. Jennifer Kostic, Associate Dean for the School of Nursing Felician University 262 South Main Street Lodi, New Jersey 07644 Salary: Commensurate with experience. About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Spec