ram that is right for you in the School of Arts and Sciences, School of Business and Information Sciences, Education, Nursing, or the Institute for Information Sciences. School of Arts & Sciences School of Education School of Business and Information Sciences School of Nursing The Felician Advantage Lenke Family Center for Innovation Center for Career & Academic Success Center for Academic Technology Honors Program STEM Office of the Registrar Catalogs Institutional Review Board Summer Programs Academic Events Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid at Felician University Inspiring courses that make you think, dedicated faculty who will push you further than you imagined, and hands-on experiences that will shape your career and future. No SAT/ACT Required Affordability Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Adult Undergraduate Admissions Transfer Admissions Our Admissions Representatives High School Guidance Counselor Portal Accepted Students International Students Veterans Services Student Financial Services Make Application Payment Parents Virtual and On Campus Tours Become a Corporate Partner Virtual Appointments Admission Events Campus Life Campus Life at Felician University Our goal is to provide our students with a quality out of class experience that supports and amplifies the teaching and learning process which is the heart of our University. Students may choose from a wide range of opportunities which are designed to help them develop their leadership abilities and to have an enjoyable collegiate experience with great memories that will never end. Office of Student Affairs Dining Services Student Handbook Technology Services Students with Disabilities Residence Life The Center for Student Development and Engagement Campus Safety Counseling and Wellness Services Title IX Campus Ministry University Library University Bookstore Emergency Telephone Numbers Parents Bus & Shuttle Schedules Athletics GET INFO VISIT APPLY Home \\ About Felician University \\ Careers at Felician JV Men’s Soccer Coach and Athletics Coordinator Junior Varsity Men’s Soccer Coach and Athletics Coordinator Felician University is presently offering an exciting opportunity for an energetic and goal-oriented individual with coaching experience in collegiate men’s soccer to serve as the Junior Varsity Men’s Soccer Coach and Athletics Coordinator. Reporting to the Assistant Director of External Operations, the Junior Varsity Men’s Soccer Coach  and Athletic Coordinator is responsible for the training, direction and supervision of the student athletes participating in the Junior Varsity Men’s Soccer Program, as well as the execution of the operational aspects of the program. S/he supports the Assistant Director of Athletics – Facilities & Operations on the day-to-day management of all aspects for the Department of Athletics, including but not limited to: travel, lodging, and meal needs as well as the coordination of departmental purchases. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. We offer a choice of medical, dental, vision, and life insurance benefits, as well as a retirement plan (403B), tuition remission, and generous time off benefits. Required Education: Bachelor’s degree in related field required; Master’s degree preferred Qualifications: Minimum 1-2 years’ experience working in facilities or equipment management, preferably in an institutions of higher education. Professional appearance and demeanor; ability and willingness to serve as a role model for student athletes. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Well-developed organizational skills, detail-oriented. Excellent physical condition, with the ability to lift up to 50 lbs. Ability and willingness to work a flexible schedule including weekends and evenings. Demonstrated ability to work with students of diverse backgrounds and experience levels. Ability and willingness to support and promote the Franciscan Felician mission and values of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume and contact information for at least 3 professional references electronically to: Assistant Director or via USPS to: Mr. Brandon Levine, Assistant Director Felician University 1 Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 Salary: $45,000 – 50,000  Commensurate with experience About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Assistant Professor, Cybersecurity and Computer Sciences Assistant Professor, Management and Entrepreneurial Studies Assistant Professor, Marketing Assistant Professor, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Sports Information Director and Intramurals Coordinator Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant/Associate Professor, Mathematics Associate Director for Academic Operations Associate Director of Housing Operations Associate Director of Student Accounts Associate Director of Student Financial Services Operations Associate Director of Transfer Student Success Associate Professor – PsyD Counseling Psychology Program Attitude Against Violence Project Coordinator Building and Grounds Assis