l Time Faculty, Mathematics Full Time Faculty, Mathematics Felician University, the Franciscan University of New Jersey, seeks an academically qualified specialist to serve as Assistant/Associate Professor of Mathematics in the School of Arts and Sciences for the 2026-2027 academic year. Candidates should have experience teaching in a traditional and online environment and must be willing to pursue Felician online certification.  S/he must possess comprehensive mathematical expertise to teach across the complete spectrum of undergraduate mathematics courses, from developmental and foundational courses through advanced upper-level offerings required for the bachelor’s degree in mathematics. S/he will serve students at all levels of mathematical preparation utilizing exceptional communication skills to make complex mathematical concepts accessible and engaging for diverse learners. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. We offer a  choice of medical, dental, vision, and life insurance benefits, as well as a retirement plan (403B), tuition remission, and generous time off benefits. Position Type: Full-time, 10-months, Exempt Department: Mathematics, School of Arts and Sciences Required Education: Earned doctoral degree in Mathematics or related field such as Mathematics Education or Applied Mathematics Qualifications: Demonstrated expertise across the full spectrum of undergraduate mathematics curriculum from developmental through advanced coursework. Minimum of two years teaching experience in mathematics at the college level. Strong verbal and written communication skills with proven ability to explain complex mathematical concepts clearly and effectively. Demonstrated skill in working with students of diverse academic backgrounds and learning styles. Proficiency with mathematical software, learning management systems, and educational technology tools. Ability to adapt teaching methods to accommodate different learning preferences and academic preparation levels. Strong organizational and time management skills. Commitment to fostering an inclusive and supportive learning environment for all students. Ability and willingness to support and promote the Felician Franciscan core values and mission of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, current curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information for two professional references electronically to the Associate Dean or via USPS to: Dr. Gaby Fahmy, Associate Dean School of Arts and Sciences Felician University 262 South Main Street Lodi, New Jersey 07644 Salary: $67,100 – 74,700 Commensurate with rank and experience About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Assistant Professor, Cybersecurity and Computer Sciences Assistant Professor, Management and Entrepreneurial Studies Assistant Professor, Marketing Assistant Professor, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Sports Information Director and Intramurals Coordinator Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant/Associate Professor, Mathematics Associate Director f