\\ Careers at Felician Assistant Professor, Cybersecurity and Computer Sciences Felician University is presently offering an exciting opportunity for an academically qualified, full-time faculty with expertise in both computer science/cybersecurity and criminal justice. The candidate should have a Ph.D. in a relevant field, criminal justice credentials, and a proven track record of teaching excellence. S/he should be comfortable developing and delivering courses across various formats (in-person, hybrid, online), as well as strong research skills and a passion for publishing. The Assistant Professor will be expected to participate in university events, student advisement, assessment, and curriculum development.  Excellent communication skills and a commitment to professional growth are essential.  Kowledge of at least two programming languages is required, and CISSP certification preferred. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. We offer a choice of medical, dental, vision, and life insurance benefits, as well as a retirement plan (403B), tuition remission, and generous time off benefits. Required Education: Earned doctoral degree in computer science/cybersecurity and credentials in related criminal justice or cybersecurity fields required; MS in cybersecurity, with certifications and work in cybersecurity industry may be considered Qualifications: Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching and research. Provide evidence of effective teaching (student evaluations, peer evaluations); demonstrated expertise in the areas of cybercrime and computer science/cybersecurity, as well as prior experience with course development related to cybercrime and cybersecurity, including fully online and/or hybrid course development and teaching; extensive knowledge in the area of cybercrime including computer hacking, digital piracy, electronic fraud and theft, and other forms of victimization; experience in cross-disciplinary research and programs integrating criminal justice with computer science/cybersecurity; superior written and verbal communications skills; CISSP certification preferred; working knowledge of at least two programming languages as well as practical and/or teaching experience in subjects such as network security; willingness and ability to support the Felician Franciscan mission and core values of the university. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume, and 3 professional references electronically to: Associate Dean or via USPS to: Dr. David Turi, Associate Dean School of Business and Information Sciences Felician University 1 Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 Salary: Commensurate with rank and experience. About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Assistant Professor, Cybersecurity and Computer Sciences Assistant Professor, Management and Entrepreneurial Studies Assistant Professor, Marketing Assistant Professor, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Sports Information Director and Intramurals Coordinator Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant/Associa