Felician Associate Director for Academic Operations Felician University, the Franciscan University of New Jersey is seeking a dynamic, creative, and enthusiastic office operations professional to serve as Associate Director of Academic operations. The Associate Director has oversight of a variety of office functions, and ensures the efficient and effective management of academic operations within the Office of Registration and Records. S/he has oversight for a wide breadth and depth of education support services. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. We offer a choice of medical, dental, vision, and life insurance benefits, as well as a retirement plan (403B), tuition remission, and generous time off benefits. Required Education: BA/BS degree required, Master’s degree in higher education administration, educational leadership, or related field preferred Qualifications: 3+ years of experience in higher education; preferably in the Registrar & Records area; knowledge of the Ellucian Colleague database and SIS databases; comprehensive understanding of FERPA regulations governing privacy rights concerning student records; excellent communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills; ability to work both independently and as part of a team; in-depth knowledge of best practices, trends, regulatory requirements of academic operations, student records management; knowledge of and significant experience with Microsoft Office Suite; proven ability to think strategically. And with a strong operational function; ability and willingness to train co-workers and students on new technologies; ability and willingness to support and promote the Felician Franciscan mission and values of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, current curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information for (two) 2 professional references electronically to: Director or via USPS to: Ms. Erminda Velez-Quinones, Director Office of Registration and Records Felician University 262 South Main Street Lodi, New Jersey 07644 About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Assistant Professor, Cybersecurity and Computer Sciences Assistant Professor, Management and Entrepreneurial Studies Assistant Professor, Marketing Assistant Professor, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Sports Information Director and Intramurals Coordinator Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant/Associate Professor, Mathematics Associate Director for Academic Operations Associate Director of Housing Operations Associate Director of Student Accounts Associate Director of Student Financial Services Operations Associate Director of Transfer Student Success Associate Professor – PsyD Counseling Psychology Program Attitude Against Violence Project Coordinator Building and Grounds Assistant Campus Security: Part-time Security Officer Clinical Adjunct Faculty, Hybrid ABSN, Parsippany, School of Nursing Clinical Adjunct Faculty, School of Nursing, Traditional ABSN, Rutherfod NJ Director of Institutional Assessment and Accreditation 