stant Coach, Men’s Soccer Felician University is currently offering an exciting opportunity for a dynamic, energic, enthusiastic and experienced athletics professional to serve as Assistant Coach for Men’s Soccer.  The Assistant Coach is responsible for supporting the Head Coach with all aspects of the Men’s Soccer program at the University, with primary responsibility for teaching and training student-athletes in the rules, regulations, equipment needs, skills and techniques of soccer. The position is  a fully in-person, part-time appointment not to exceed 25 hours per week. Position Type: Part-time, 12-months, Exempt Department: Athletics Education Requiements: Bachelor’s degree required. Degree requirement may be waived with significant relative practical coaching experience. Qualifications: Minimum of 1-year collegiate coaching experience in soccer or related sport; strong written and verbal communications skills; proven ability to engage, motivate and direct a team of student athletes of diverse backgrounds and experience levels; detail-oriented; ability to instruct skills associated with soccer; ability and willingness to work a flexible schedule which includes evenings and weekends; ability to support and promote the Franciscan Felician mission and values of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume and 2 professional references electronically to the Head Coach or via USPS to Mr. Brandon Levine, Head Coach Felician University Athletics 1 Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant