 University \\ Careers at Felician Clinical Adjunct Faculty, Hybrid ABSN, Parsippany, School of Nursing Felician University is offering exciting opportunities for Clinical Adjunct Faculty in the School of Nursing for the Fall 2026 semester at our state-of-the-arts Parsippany location. Clinical Adjuncts oversee the clinical education of Prelicensure BSN nursing students with responsibility for evaluating the clinical experience of students and grading clinical assignments. They collaborate closely with the course lead to ensure that clinical learning objectives are achieved. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. Position Type: Part-time, 1-2 courses per semester, maximum 3 days per week. Department: School of Nursing, Hybrid Prelicensure BSN Program Required Education: Master’s degree in nursing Qualifications: Current New Jersey RN license in good standing; current certification in CPR; experience teaching at the baccalaureate level; willingness and ability to support and promote the Felician Franciscan core values and mission of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, current curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information for two professional references electronically to the Associate Dean or via USPS to: Dr. Erin Vitale, Associate Dean Hybrid ABSN School of Nursing Felician University 262 South Main Street Lodi, New Jersey 07644 Salary: $80.00/hour About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assis