t is right for you in the School of Arts and Sciences, School of Business and Information Sciences, Education, Nursing, or the Institute for Information Sciences. School of Arts & Sciences School of Education School of Business and Information Sciences School of Nursing The Felician Advantage Lenke Family Center for Innovation Center for Career & Academic Success Center for Academic Technology Honors Program STEM Office of the Registrar Catalogs Institutional Review Board Summer Programs Academic Events Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid at Felician University Inspiring courses that make you think, dedicated faculty who will push you further than you imagined, and hands-on experiences that will shape your career and future. No SAT/ACT Required Affordability Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Adult Undergraduate Admissions Transfer Admissions Our Admissions Representatives High School Guidance Counselor Portal Accepted Students International Students Veterans Services Student Financial Services Make Application Payment Parents Virtual and On Campus Tours Become a Corporate Partner Virtual Appointments Admission Events Campus Life Campus Life at Felician University Our goal is to provide our students with a quality out of class experience that supports and amplifies the teaching and learning process which is the heart of our University. Students may choose from a wide range of opportunities which are designed to help them develop their leadership abilities and to have an enjoyable collegiate experience with great memories that will never end. Office of Student Affairs Dining Services Student Handbook Technology Services Students with Disabilities Residence Life The Center for Student Development and Engagement Campus Safety Counseling and Wellness Services Title IX Campus Ministry University Library University Bookstore Emergency Telephone Numbers Parents Bus & Shuttle Schedules Athletics GET INFO VISIT APPLY Home \\ About Felician University \\ Careers at Felician Associate Director of Housing Operations Felician University is presently seeking an experienced, highly motivated, creative, self-motivated, and student-centric student residential life professional to serve as Associate Director for Housing Operations.  Reporting to the Director of Housing and Residence Life, the Associate Director assumes a major leadership role in providing a sense of community within the residential halls and has overall responsibility for developing and administering a comprehensive residential community educational program as well as maintaining the safe and comfortable living environment that meets the goals of the university. The Associate Director for Residential Education and Development is required to live on campus and be a visible presence during and outside of office hours, including evenings and weekends. S/he will be provided an unfurnished, one-bedroom apartment. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. We offer a  choice of medical, dental, vision, and life insurance benefits, as well as a retirement plan (403B), tuition remission, and generous time off benefits. Required Education: BA/BS degree required, Master’s degree in Higher Education/College Student Personnel or related field preferred. Qualifications: 2+ years of full-time, progressive professional, experience managing overall operations of residential life and housing that includes: housing policies and processes; mentoring students, safety programs, alcohol awareness programs, educational programming, recreation and social programs and orientation programs, policy development, marketing, managing staff, budgeting, billing, damage assessments and safety; demonstrated supervisory, administrative, organizations skills; superior written and verbal communications skills; proven ability to manage stress; conflict, and frustration constructively; positive attitude with the ability to serve as a role model for students in attitude and conduct; experience in conflict resolution and mediation in a residence hall setting; comprehensive knowledge of effective methods for managing/coaching diverse populations of students; proven ability to work both autonomously and as part of a team; ability to prioritize and manage multiple challenging projects, tasks and situations;  willingness and availability to work a flex schedule as an on-call professional, including nights and weekends (extended vacations limited to published University break schedule); willing ness and ability to embrace new technologies and innovative organizational practices; knowledge of or the ability to learn quickly Felician University software programs such as eRezLife, Colleague, Maxient, and Microsoft Office; ability to support and promote the Felician Franciscan mission and core values of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume and 2 professional references electronically to: Director or via USPS to: Ms. Onya Brown, Associate Dean for Student Affairs Felician University 1 Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 Salary Range:  $53.5 – 71.1, commensurate with education, certifications and experience About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Assist