an Part-Time Professional Science Tutor Felician University is presently seeking an experienced professional to serve as part-time Science Tutor in the Center for Academic Success and Effectiveness.  The Tutor facilitates student learning by helping to clarify specific course content and promoting/modeling the use of appropriate study strategies. He/she is responsible for the development and integration of effective study and learning strategies to maximize student potential for independent learning and academic progress. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. We offer tuition remission, and generous time off benefits. Required Education: BS in Science discipline required; Master’s degree preferred Qualifications: Relevant work experience that demonstrates the ability to relate to and engage with students as a tutor; proven ability to work well with a diverse student population; creative thinking, problem-solving and analytical skills; a collaborative spirit; willingness and ability to support and promote the Felician Franciscan mission and values. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume and 3 professional references electronically to: Coordinator or via USPS to: Mr. Lloyd Cutkelvin Center for Academic Success and Experiential Learning Felician University 262 South Main Street Lodi, New Jersey 07644 About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of U