an University \\ Careers at Felician Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services IN THIS SECTION About Felician University Summer Sports and Gaming Camps Board of Trustees Members Institutional Assessment Accreditations Middle States Self-Study Process Strategic Plan Fast Facts Careers at Felician Associate Director of Student Financial Services Operations Full-time Faculty – School of Nursing Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Program Analyst – Information Systems Faculty Adjunct – Graduate Nursing Assistant/Associate Professor, Mathematics Part-time Assistant Coach, Men’s Wrestling Associate Director of Student Accounts Clinical Adjunct Faculty, School of Nursing, Traditional ABSN, Rutherfod NJ Assistant Professor, Prelicensure Nursing Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Part-Time ESL Instructors  July 15-August 5, 2026 Faculty Adjuncts, Philosophy Security Officers Faculty Adjuncts, School of Business and Information Sciences Instructor, School of Nursing Faculty Adjunct, Communications Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Academic Success Coach JV Men’s Soccer Coach and Athletics Coordinator Full Time Faculty, Mathematics Assistant Professor, Cybersecurity and Computer Sciences Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Associate Director for Academic Operations Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Clinical Adjunct Faculty, Hybrid ABSN, Parsippany, School of Nursing Associate Director of Housing Operations Associate Director of Transfer Student Success Part-Time Professional Science Tutor Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Building and Grounds Assistant Attitude Against Violence Project Coordinator Assistant/Associate Professor, Chemistry Head Coach, Women’s Acrobatics and Tumbling Assistant Professor, Marketing Assessment Data Coordinator Engagement and Philanthropy Officer Director of Internships and Assessment, School of Education Assistant Sports Information Director and Intramurals Coordinator Assistant Professor, Management and Entrepreneurial Studies Head Coach, Men’s Soccer Head Coach, eSports Prelicensure Nursing Program, Parsippany NJ – Clinical Adjunct Faculty Associate Professor – PsyD Counseling Psychology Program Campus Security: Part-time Security Officer Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Management/Entrepreneurial Studies Faculty Inter-Campus Shuttle Bus Drivers Inter-Campus Shuttle Bus Drivers Half-Time Instructor, Prelicensure Nursing IT Help Desk Support Technician – Temporary Director of Institutional Assessment and Accreditation Full-time Faculty, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Evening and Weekend Circulation Supervisor Research and Instruction Librarian Faculty Adjunct – Mathematics Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Adjunct Faculty, English Conference and Event Services Directions & Maps On Campus Tours History & Tradition Office of the President Senior Administrative Officers Alumni REED Autism Services Partnership Felician University, the Franciscan University of New Jersey is seeking dynamic, enthusiastic and highly organized full-time professional Administrative Assistant to provide support to the Dean. The Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services is a full-time, in-person, 12-month position with two co-equal areas of responsibility. The role provides direct administrative and operational support to the Dean of Student Success, Retention, & Assessment, including coordination of the Dean’s schedule, communications, meetings, records, reporting, purchasing, events, and assigned priorities.  The role also supports the Office of Accessibility Services, providing administrative and logistical support for approved accommodations, testing coordination, student and faculty communications, confidential records, and related service workflows in partnership with the Coordinator of Accessibility Services. The position serves as a primary point of contact for the Dean’s office and accessibility services and requires exceptional organization, attention to detail, sound judgment, discretion in handling confidential information, and a commitment to responsive, student-centered service and the University mission. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. Required Education: Associate degree and a minimum of three years of progressively responsible administrative experience required, BA/BS preferred Qualifications: Relevant experience in higher education, student services, accessibility services, or a similar service environment is preferred; demonstrated reliability, initiative, sound judgment, attention to detail, and commitment to responsive, student-centered service; demonstrated ability to adapt to changing priorities, procedures, technologies, and service needs while managing competing responsibilities effectively; demonstrated ability to collaborate and communicate effectively, professionally, and with appropriate discretion when serving students, faculty, staff, families, and campus partners; demonstrated ability to handle confidential student information with discretion and to maintain accurate, secure records in accordance with University policies and established procedures; demonstrated organizational skills and ability to manage multiple calendars, deadlines, records, service requests, and competing priorities accurately across two functional assignments; proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, including Excel, Word, and Outlook, and the ability to use University information systems; accessibility-related platforms, and web-based tools to manage scheduling, communications, records, reporting, and service workflows;  willingness and ability to master new computer programs, including student support, accessibility-related, and administrative systems; willingness and ability to support and promote the Felician Franciscan mission and core values of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, current curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information for (two) 2 professional references electronically to: Dean via USPS to: Dr. Jeffrey Blanchard, Dean, Center for Academic Success & Effectiveness Felician University 1 Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Assistant Professor, Cybersecurity and Computer Sciences Assistant Professor, Management and Entrepreneurial Studies Assistant Professor, Marketing Assistant Professor, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Sports Information Director and Intramurals Coordinator Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant/Associate Professor, Mathematics Associate Director for Academic Operations Associate Director of Housing Operations Associate Director of Student Accounts Associate Director of Student Financial Services Operations Associate Director of Transfer Student Success Associate Professor – PsyD Counseling Psychology Program Attitude Against Violence Project Coordinator Building and Grounds Assistant Campus Security: Part-time Security Officer Clinical Adjunct Faculty, Hybrid ABSN, Parsippany, School of Nursing Clinical Adjunct Faculty, School of Nursing, Traditional ABSN, Rutherfod NJ Director of Institutional Assessment and Accreditation Director of Internships and Assessment, School of Education Engagement and Philanthropy Officer Evening and Weekend Circulation Supervisor Faculty Adjunct – Mathematics Faculty Adjunct – Graduate Nursing Faculty Adjunct, Communications Faculty Adjuncts, Philosophy Faculty Adjuncts, School of Business and Information Sciences Full Time Faculty, Mathematics Full-time Faculty – School of Nursing Full-time Faculty, Prelicensure Nursing Half-Time Instructor, Prelicensure Nursing Head Coach, eSports Head Coach, Men’s Soccer Head Coach, Women’s Acrobatics and Tumbling Instructor, School of Nursing Inter-Campus Shuttle Bus Drivers Inter-Campus Shuttle Bus Drivers IT Help Desk Support Technician – Temporary JV Men’s Soccer Coach and Athletics Coordinator Management/Entrepreneurial Studies Faculty Part-time Assistant Coach, Men’s Wrestling Part-Time ESL Instructors  July 15-August 5, 2026 Part-Time Professional Science Tutor Prelicensure Nursing Program, Parsippany NJ – Clinical Adjunct Faculty Program Analyst – Information Systems Research and Instruction Librarian Security Officers Conference and Event Services Directions & Maps Fast Facts History & Tradition Felician Franciscan Ministry Institutional Assessment Institutional Assessment Plan Mission, Values, and Objectives Middle States Self-Study Process Co-Chairs for Working Groups Communication Plan Institutional Priorities Intended Outcomes Self-Study Design Strategic Plan 2025-2028 Timetable for Middle States Updates Working Group Charges Office of the President History of the 