at Felician Attitude Against Violence Project Coordinator IN THIS SECTION About Felician University Summer Sports and Gaming Camps Board of Trustees Members Institutional Assessment Accreditations Middle States Self-Study Process Strategic Plan Fast Facts Careers at Felician Associate Director of Student Financial Services Operations Full-time Faculty – School of Nursing Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Program Analyst – Information Systems Faculty Adjunct – Graduate Nursing Assistant/Associate Professor, Mathematics Part-time Assistant Coach, Men’s Wrestling Associate Director of Student Accounts Clinical Adjunct Faculty, School of Nursing, Traditional ABSN, Rutherfod NJ Assistant Professor, Prelicensure Nursing Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Part-Time ESL Instructors  July 15-August 5, 2026 Faculty Adjuncts, Philosophy Security Officers Faculty Adjuncts, School of Business and Information Sciences Instructor, School of Nursing Faculty Adjunct, Communications Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Academic Success Coach JV Men’s Soccer Coach and Athletics Coordinator Full Time Faculty, Mathematics Assistant Professor, Cybersecurity and Computer Sciences Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Associate Director for Academic Operations Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Clinical Adjunct Faculty, Hybrid ABSN, Parsippany, School of Nursing Associate Director of Housing Operations Associate Director of Transfer Student Success Part-Time Professional Science Tutor Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Building and Grounds Assistant Attitude Against Violence Project Coordinator Assistant/Associate Professor, Chemistry Head Coach, Women’s Acrobatics and Tumbling Assistant Professor, Marketing Assessment Data Coordinator Engagement and Philanthropy Officer Director of Internships and Assessment, School of Education Assistant Sports Information Director and Intramurals Coordinator Assistant Professor, Management and Entrepreneurial Studies Head Coach, Men’s Soccer Head Coach, eSports Prelicensure Nursing Program, Parsippany NJ – Clinical Adjunct Faculty Associate Professor – PsyD Counseling Psychology Program Campus Security: Part-time Security Officer Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Management/Entrepreneurial Studies Faculty Inter-Campus Shuttle Bus Drivers Inter-Campus Shuttle Bus Drivers Half-Time Instructor, Prelicensure Nursing IT Help Desk Support Technician – Temporary Director of Institutional Assessment and Accreditation Full-time Faculty, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Evening and Weekend Circulation Supervisor Research and Instruction Librarian Faculty Adjunct – Mathematics Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Adjunct Faculty, English Conference and Event Services Directions & Maps On Campus Tours History & Tradition Office of the President Senior Administrative Officers Alumni REED Autism Services Partnership Felician University is presently seeking dedicated, knowledgeable and experienced  professional to serve as the Attitudes Against Violence Project Coordinator.  The Project Coordinator for the Attitudes Against Violence project will provide programmatic coordination for the $300,000 grant funded by the Office on Violence Against Women (OVW), U.S. Department of Justice, implemented by the Division of Student Affairs. The grant funds sexual violence prevention and education initiatives at the Felician University. He/she administers a variety of trainings and education programming events designed to education, train and change student’s attitudes towards sexual violence and intervention. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. We offer a choice of medical, dental, vision, and life insurance benefits, as well as a retirement plan (403B), tuition remission, and generous time off benefits. Position Type: Full-time, 8 months, Non-exempt Education: Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree in counseling, education, student affairs personnel administration, psychology, or related field preferred. Qualifications: 1+ years’ experience in the field of sexual assault prevention, education, counseling or a related discipline. Demonstrated leadership skills. Superior group facilitation skills. Comprehensive knowledge of legislation involving violence against women issues; Well-developed verbal and written communication skills. Willingness and ability to mentor and instruct students. Proven experience in the utilization of innovative approaches to address sexual violence. Demonstrated experience in and commitment to promoting and enhancing diversity. Ability to work autonomously, particularly in the areas of program development and management. Ability and willingness to travel and work evenings/weekends as needed. Program experience in student affairs preferred. Ability and willingness to support and promote the Felician Franciscan mission and vales of the University. Send cover letter, resume and 3 professional references electronically to: Director or via USPS to: Dr. Simone Taylor Director of Community Rights and Responsibilities Felician University 1 Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 Salary: Commensurate with experience About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assist