lician Assistant/Associate Professor, Chemistry Felician University is presently seeking an academically qualified educator to serve as Assistant/ Associate Professor in Chemistry in the department of Natural Sciences.  The Assistant/Associate Professor provides instruction in the fundamentals of the respective discipline, as well as incorporate real-world experience. Teaching responsibilities will include a traditional and, preferably, also an online educational environment, with Felician online certification required for the latter. Position Type: Full-Time, 10-Month, Exempt Department: School of Arts and Sciences, Department of Natural Sciences Date Posted: April 19, 2021 Required Education: Master’s degree in Chemistry or a related area required; doctoral degree preferred. ABD will be considered. Qualifications: Minimum of 3 years’ experience in teaching at an institution of higher education; demonstrated experience working with a multicultural and highly diverse student population; ability and willingness to successfully complete Felician University online certification; ability and willingness to support and promote the Franciscan Felician mission and values of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume and 3 professional references electronically to : Dean or via USPS to: Dr. Mildred Mihlon, Dean School of Arts & Sciences Felician University 262 South Main Street Lodi, New Jersey 07644 About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Dev