 Felician Head Coach, Women’s Acrobatics and Tumbling Felician University is currently offering an exciting opportunity for a dynamic, energetic, enthusiastic and experienced athletics professional to serve as Head Coach and Athletics Coordinator for our newly organized Women’s Acrobatics and Tumbling team.  The Head Coach is responsible for the instruction of our acrobatics and tumbling team members in the rules and regulations, equipment needs and care, performance skill set and safety measures associated with the sport of acrobatics and tumbling. S/he will assist the Director of Athletics in the management of the Women’s Acrobatics and Tumbling Program, recruitment of student athletes, site supervision of home events and other aspects of departmental administration. Position Type: Full-time, 12-months, Exempt Department: Enrollment Management Division, Athletics Department Date Posted: July 27, 2022 Required Education: Bachelor’s degree required, Master’s degree preferred Qualifications: Proven experience in coaching women’s acrobatics and tumbling or gymnastics; 2+ years’ experience in athletics facilities or equipment management, preferably in an institution of higher learning; well-developed written and verbal communications skills; proven ability to engage, motivate and direct a team of student athletes of diverse backgrounds and experience levels; detail-oriented; ability to instruct skills associated with acrobatics and tumbling competition; excellent physical condition, with the ability to lift up to 50 pounds; ability and willingness to work a flexible schedule which includes evenings and weekends; ability to support and promote the Franciscan Felician mission and values of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume and 2 professional references electronically to Interim Director or via USPS to Mr. Andrew Toriello, Interim Director Felician University Athletics 1 Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 Salary: Commensurate with experience About