istant Professor, Marketing The School of Business and Information Sciences of Felician University is presently offering an exciting opportunity for an academically qualified, full-time Marketing faculty to develop and deliver undergraduate courses, integrating analytics and using simulations.  The Assistant Professor will be responsible to teach, administer, and develop curriculum across its undergraduate and graduate business programs, and will fulfill all responsibilities of a full-time faculty member in the areas of Teaching Effectiveness, Scholarship, and Service as outlined in the Felician University Faculty Handbook. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. We offer a choice of medical, dental, vision, and life insurance benefits, as well as a retirement plan (403B), tuition remission, and generous time off benefits. Position Type: Full-Time, 10-month, Exempt Department: School of Business and Information Sciences Required Education: Earned doctoral degree required Qualifications: 2+ years’ experience teaching at both undergraduate and graduate courses; proven ability to create engaging learning experiences across traditional, online and hybrid environments; ability and willingness to teach at off-sites campus sites as needed;  demonstrated familiarity with assessment and willingness to  participate in assessment training; comprehensive knowledge of marketing, data analytics, simulation software and emerging industry trends; ability to design and implement courses that integrate data analytics concepts with marketing theory to provide students with practical, data-driven skills; proven ability to utilize simulation tools  to enhance student learning and engagement with marketing principles; demonstrated familiarity with BrightSpace LMS or other LMS tools; exceptional communications and interpersonal skills; ability to engage effectively with a diverse constituency of traditional and non-traditional students; demonstrated ability to build and support interdivisional relationships and collaborate with  diverse groups of staff, faculty and external stakeholders; willingness and ability to support the Felician Franciscan mission and core values of the university. To Apply: Send cover letter, current curriculum vitae, resume, 3 professional references and three prior classroom evaluations related to marketing courses taught electronically to: School of Business or via USPS to: Ms. Patricia McTaggart School of Business and Information Sciences Felician University 1 Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 Salary: Commensurate with rank and experience. Start Date: Review of candidate materials will start immediately.  All materials due on or before June 15, 2024.  Position start date is August 12, 2024. About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Assistant Professor, Cybersecurity and Computer Sciences Assistant Professor, Management and Entrepreneurial Studies Assistant Professor, Marketing Assistant Professor, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Sports Information Director and Intramurals Coordinator Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Assistant/Associate Profess