r you in the School of Arts and Sciences, School of Business and Information Sciences, Education, Nursing, or the Institute for Information Sciences. School of Arts & Sciences School of Education School of Business and Information Sciences School of Nursing The Felician Advantage Lenke Family Center for Innovation Center for Career & Academic Success Center for Academic Technology Honors Program STEM Office of the Registrar Catalogs Institutional Review Board Summer Programs Academic Events Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid at Felician University Inspiring courses that make you think, dedicated faculty who will push you further than you imagined, and hands-on experiences that will shape your career and future. No SAT/ACT Required Affordability Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Adult Undergraduate Admissions Transfer Admissions Our Admissions Representatives High School Guidance Counselor Portal Accepted Students International Students Veterans Services Student Financial Services Make Application Payment Parents Virtual and On Campus Tours Become a Corporate Partner Virtual Appointments Admission Events Campus Life Campus Life at Felician University Our goal is to provide our students with a quality out of class experience that supports and amplifies the teaching and learning process which is the heart of our University. Students may choose from a wide range of opportunities which are designed to help them develop their leadership abilities and to have an enjoyable collegiate experience with great memories that will never end. Office of Student Affairs Dining Services Student Handbook Technology Services Students with Disabilities Residence Life The Center for Student Development and Engagement Campus Safety Counseling and Wellness Services Title IX Campus Ministry University Library University Bookstore Emergency Telephone Numbers Parents Bus & Shuttle Schedules Athletics GET INFO VISIT APPLY Home \\ About Felician University \\ Careers at Felician Assessment Data Coordinator Felician University is presently seeking an industrious, focused, innovative and analytically-minded professional to serve as the Assessment Data Coordinator in the Center for Academic Success and Effectiveness.  The Coordinator is responsible for providing data support for the multiple platforms run out of the Center in order to help improve assessment and overall student and faculty success.  S/he collaborates with faculty, staff, and administration to support assessment initiatives as well as annual assessment efforts, facilitates reporting across assessment platforms to provide usable data, provides evidence for decision-making across the university, and helps foster a culture of assessment. Position Type: Full-time, 12-month, Non-exempt Department: Center for Academic Success and Effectiveness Required Education: Bachelor’s Degree required. Qualifications: Minimum of 1 year of data management and systems administration experience; demonstrated experience with assessment, assessment platforms, Learning Management Systems, course survey instruments;  attention to detail, strong organizational skills, effective communication skills, including the ability to communicate technical information in oral, written, and graphic form to individuals with varying backgrounds; proven ability to maintain confidentiality in regard to information processed, stored, or accessed by the system; proficiency with Office  Suite applications (Excel, Word, PowerPoint); emotional intelligence, self-awareness, self-critique, and social skills;  demonstrated ability to work effectively in a collaborative environment; ability to build rapport with others and actively listen to the concerns and opinions of others; willingness and ability to support and promote the Felician Franciscan mission and core values of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume and 3 professional references electronically to: Dean or via USPS to: Dr. Jeffery Blanchard, Dean of the Center for Academic Success and Effectiveness Felician University 262 South Main Street Lodi, New Jersey 07644 Salary: Commensurate with experience About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Assistant Professor, Cybersecurity and Computer Sciences Assistant Professor, Management and Entrepreneurial Studies Assistant Professor, Marketing Assistant Professor, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Sports Information Director and Intramurals Coordinator Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant/Associate Professor, Mathematics Associate Director for Academic Operations Associate Director of Housing Operations Associate Director of Student Accounts Associate Director of Student Financial Services Operations Associate Director of Transfer Student Success Associate Professor – PsyD Counseling Psychology Program Attitude Against Violence Project Coordinator Building and Grounds Assistant Campus Security: Part-time Security Officer Clinical Adjunct Faculty, Hybrid ABSN, Parsippany, School of Nursing Clinical Adjunct Faculty, School of Nursing, Traditional ABSN, Rutherfod NJ Director of Institutional Assessment and Accreditation Director of Internships and Assessment, School of Education Engagement and P