n Engagement and Philanthropy Officer Felician University, the Franciscan University of New Jersey is offering an exciting opportunity for an experienced development professional to join our dynamic advancement team as an Engagement and Philanthropy Officer!  The EPO is responsible for engaging current and prospective supporters of assigned Schools within the University, developing gift and partnership solicitations, cultivating new and assigned prospects, stewardship and developing and executing special events to engage donors and partnerships. S/he is accountable for creating opportunities to support the University’s academic and program priorities among alumni, donors, parents and external funding partners. Position Type: Full time, 12-month, Exempt Department: University Advancement Date Posted: Thursday, July 28, 2022 Required Education: Bachelor’s degree required Qualifications: 3+ years’ of related fundraising , alumni engagement or external relations experience; 2+ years’ experience with project management; intermediate level proficiency with Microsoft Office and 365 applications; well-developed written and verbal communications skills; proven presentation skills, ability to communicate vision and content to diverse constituencies, including but not limited to students, staff, faculty, potential donors and other external stakeholders; demonstrated enthusiasm, energy and passion for the support and promotion of opportunities at the University;  strong collaborative skills, ability to develop, foster and maintain effective working relationships with a diverse group of internal and external partners; demonstrated success in team building; ability to multi-task and adapt expediently to changing priorities and conditions; ability to maintain emotional balance and effectively address unusual and/or unexpected situations during the course of work; “can do” assertive philosophy; willingness and ability to support and promote the Felician Franciscan mission and values of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume, and the names and contact information for (two) 2 professional references electronically to the Office of the Vice President o r via USPS to: Ms. Carol Martinez, Office of the Vice President University Advancement Felician University 1 Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 Salary: Commensurate with experience. About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Assistant Professor, Cybersecurity and Computer Sciences Assistant Professor, Management and Entrepreneurial Studies Assistant Professor, Marketing Assistant Professor, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Sports Information Director and Intramurals Coordinator Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant/Associate Professor, Mathematics Associate Director for Academic Operations Associate Director of Housing Operations Associate Director of Student Accounts Associate Director of Student Financial Services Operations Associate Director of Transfer Student Success Associate Professor – PsyD Counseling Psychology Program Attitude Against Violence Project Coordinator Building and Grounds Assistant Campus Security: Part-time Security Officer Clinical Adjunct Faculty, Hybrid ABSN, Parsip