ty \\ Careers at Felician Director of Internships and Assessment, School of Education Felician University, the Franciscan University of New Jersey is offering an exciting opportunity for an experienced education professional to join our dynamic school of Education team as the Director of Internships and Assessment! The Director manages all field experiences/internship placements and related certification requirements for all undergraduate and graduate programs across the various programs of the School of Education.  The Director will also be charged in being the lead on the management and collection of data for the SoE assessment system in relation to accreditation and all federal/state reporting. S/he fosters the mission and vision of the School of Education and Felician University and manages the workflow of the Office of Internship & Assessment through fulfilling the job responsibilities below, reflecting our Felician/Franciscan core values in all interactions and relationships. Position Type: Full time, 12-month, Exempt Department: School of Education Date Posted: Thursday, July 28, 2022 Required Education: Master’s degree required,  doctoral degree preferred. Qualifications: NJ issued license in good standing; proven experience working in a P12 school setting; proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, including Word, Excel, PowerPoint and Outlook; demonstrated interpersonal skills; sensitivity to and ability to engage with and direct a culturally and religiously diverse student population; strong organizational skills; well-developed verbal, written communications skills; strong presentation skills; demonstrated ability to work autonomously with multiple priorities and deadlines; demonstrated familiarity with social networking venues; willingness and ability to support and promote the Felician Franciscan mission and core values of the University; successful completion of a teacher education program and/or experience working in a K12 school setting preferred; prior experience with accreditation and data collection/reporting to professional associations; ability and willingness to support and promote the Felician Franciscan mission and core values of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume, and the names and contact information for (two) 2 professional references electronically to the Dean or via USPS to: Dr. Stephanie McGowan, Dean for the School of Education Felician University 1 Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 Salary: Commensurate with experience. About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Assistant Professor, Cybersecurity and Computer Sciences Assistant Professor, Management and Entrepreneurial Studies Assistant Professor, Marketing Assistant Professor, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Sports Information Director and Intramurals Coordinator Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant/Associate Professor, Mathematics Associate Director for Academic Operations Associate Director of Housing Operations Associate Director of Student Accounts Associate Director of Student Financial Services Operations Associate Director of Transfer Student Success Associate Professor – PsyD Counseling Psychology Program Attitude Again