iversity \\ Careers at Felician Assistant Sports Information Director and Intramurals Coordinator Felician University is currently offering an exciting opportunity for a dynamic, energic, enthusiastic and experienced athletics professional to serve as Assistant Sports Information Director and Intramural Coordinator. The Assistant Sports Information Director and Intramural Coordinator is responsible for oversight of the Intramural and Club Sport program, as well as assisting the Sports Information Director in the day-to-day management of all aspects of the Sports Information Department. Including but not limited to: social media, maintenance of the athletics website, game-day statistics and media days. Position Type: Full-time, 12-months, Exempt Department: Enrollment Management Division, Athletics Department Date Posted: July 29, 2022 Required Education: Bachelor’s degree required, Master’s degree preferred Qualifications: Minimum of 2-years’ experience working in athletics, preferably in institutions of higher educations; strong verbal and written communications skills; detail-oriented with the ability to meet deadlines; excellent physical condition, with the ability to lift up to 50 pounds; demonstrated ability to work with students of diverse backgrounds and experience levels; ability and willingness to work a flexible schedule which includes evenings and weekends; ability to support and promote the Franciscan Felician mission and values of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume and 2 professional references electronically to Interim Director or via USPS to Mr. Andrew Toriello, Interim Director Felician University Athletics 1 Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 Salary: Commensurate with experience About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Stu