 Felician Campus Security: Part-time Security Officer Felician University is presently seeking a dynamic, energetic and self-motivated security professional to safeguard the University’s facilities and enforce established security policies and procedures with University personnel, students and visitors to the campus. Position Type: Part-Time, 12-months, Non-exempt Department: Campus Safety and Security Date Posted: August 28, 2024 Required Education: High school diploma or GED required Qualifications: Minimum of one year experience in security, military or related field monitoring property and safety; prior experience in a college/university setting preferred; ability to successfully complete a University training program for certification in First Aid, CPR, and AED within 90 days of hire; Security Officer Registration Act (SORA) certification; willingness and ability to do physical labor including heavy lifting within manageable and safe parameters; occasionally lifting 25 to 50 pounds at a time. Physical ability to stand, walk, stoop, climb, bend, etc. Working conditions may include exposure to extreme temperatures (> 100 F and/or < 50 F); valid New Jersey Driver’s License; proven ability to work with a diverse population; graduation from an accredited police academy and certification by the Police Training Commission of New Jersey preferred. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume and 3 professional references electronically to:  Heath James at JamesH@felician.edu . About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admi