niversity \\ Careers at Felician Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Felician University is presently seeking an energetic and goal and student-oriented career development professional to serve as Assistant Director for the Center for Career and Professional Development.  The Assistant Director provides professional development services to students  and alumnae of Felician University, including but not limited to career development workshops, outreach programs, seminars on academics majors selection and job search and application processes. Position Type: Full-Time, 12-Month, Exempt Department: Center for Career and Professional Development Date Posted: Friday, May 21, 2021 Required Education: BA/BA in Psychology, Counseling. Social Work, Higher Education or related field required, Master’s degree preferred Qualifications: 1-3 years’ of experience providing experiential experience support in a career service department or other comparable option; career counseling or related counseling experience, preferably at an institution of higher learning; demonstrated experience managing data, forms, applications and confidential material; knowledge of online databases, especially career related databases (i.e., Simplicity, College Central Network, Handshake, and Purple Briefcase) experience preferred; proven ability to multi-task (i.e., scheduling appointments, answering phones, greeting anyone that enters the office) and successfully meet deadlines; comprehensive knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite, Prezi and social media tools (i.e., Facebook, Twitter, and LinkedIn); Desktop publishing experience preferred; ability to work collaboratively with a diverse population of students, employers, staff and faculty from multiple departments and schools; ability and willingness to work a flexible schedule, including  evenings and weekends as needed; ability and willingness to support the Franciscan Felician mission and values of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume and contact information for at least 3 professional references electronically to: Vice President for Student Affairs or via USPS to: Dr. Ronald Gray, Vice President for Student Affairs and Dean of Students Felician University 1 Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 Salary: Commensurate with experience About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Assistant Professor, Cybersecurity and Computer Sciences Assistant Professor, Management and Entrepreneurial Studies Assistant Professor, Marketing Assistant Professor, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Sports Information Director and Intramurals Coordinator Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant/Associate Professor, Mathematics Associate Director for Academic Operations Associate Director of Housing Operations Associate Director of Student Accounts Associate Director of Student Financial Services Operations Associate Director of Transfer Student Success Associate Professor – PsyD Counseling Psychology Program Attitude Against Violence Project Coordinator Building and Grounds Assistant Campus Security: Part-time Security Officer Clinical Adjunct Faculty, Hybrid ABSN, Parsippany, School of Nursing Clinical Adjunc