es Head Coach, Men’s Soccer Head Coach, eSports Prelicensure Nursing Program, Parsippany NJ – Clinical Adjunct Faculty Associate Professor – PsyD Counseling Psychology Program Campus Security: Part-time Security Officer Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Management/Entrepreneurial Studies Faculty Inter-Campus Shuttle Bus Drivers Inter-Campus Shuttle Bus Drivers Half-Time Instructor, Prelicensure Nursing IT Help Desk Support Technician – Temporary Director of Institutional Assessment and Accreditation Full-time Faculty, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Evening and Weekend Circulation Supervisor Research and Instruction Librarian Faculty Adjunct – Mathematics Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Adjunct Faculty, English Conference and Event Services Directions & Maps On Campus Tours History & Tradition Office of the President Senior Administrative Officers Alumni REED Autism Services Partnership Felician University, the Franciscan University of New Jersey, is seeking an academically qualified specialist to teach, administer and develop curriculum in its undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral business programs in the area of management/entrepreneurial studies. Candidates should have experience teaching in traditional and online environments and must be willing to pursue Felician online certification. The successful candidate has an educational background in the fundamentals of his/her discipline as well as significant practical experience to bring to class discussions and case analyses. Responsibilities will include, but are not limited to:  Teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in areas of management and entrepreneurial studies; participating in professional development activities in order to maintain currency in the primary area of teaching; contributing to student learning and development through academic advising (at both undergraduate and graduate levels, as well as mentoring doctoral students) and supporting student organizations and activities; serving on department, university, and/or community committees in support of Felician University’s mission; engaging in outcomes-based course, curriculum, and program development. Position Type: Full-time, 10-months, Exempt Department: School of Business Required Education: MBA and Ph.D./DBA required Qualifications: Experience teaching at both undergraduate and graduate levels; experience teaching in both classroom and online environments; willingness and ability to teach at off-campus sites; familiarity with assessment and willingness to participate in assessment training; communication and interpersonal skills sufficient to work effectively with a diverse array of students and colleagues; professional/industry contacts/relationships are a plus; willingness and ability to support the Felician/Franciscan values and mission. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume and 3 professional references electronically to: Associate Dean or via USPS to: Dr. David Turi, Associate Dean School of Business Felician University 1 Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 Salary: Commensurate with rank and experience About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant Professor and Academic Fiel