Felician Half-Time Instructor, Prelicensure Nursing Felician University is presently seeking an academically qualified specialist to serve as a half-time Instructor for the School of Nursing. Candidates should have experience teaching in both a traditional and online environment and are required to complete Felician University online certification. Successful candidates have an educational background in the fundamentals of their discipline as well as a wealth of real-world experience to bring to class discussions and case analyses. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. Required Education: Master’s degree in Nursing, required; doctoral degree preferred. Faculty teaching in the graduate program must have an earned doctoral degree or be enrolled in doctoral study. Qualifications: Licensure in NJ as a registered nurse, graduate faculty must have national certification and NJ Board of Nursing licensure as a Family Nurse Practitioner; practical experience in area of specialization; previous teaching experience; ability and willingness to support and promote the Franciscan Felician mission and values of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume and 3 professional references electronically to: Associate Dean or via USPS to: Dr. Patricia Munno Associate Dean, School Nursing Felician University 262 South Main Street Lodi, New Jersey 07644 Salary: Commensurate with Rank & experience About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Wo