 Felician IT Help Desk Support Technician – Temporary Felician University is presently seeking an experienced Information Technology professional to serve as a temporary Help Desk Technician from the beginning on August 10, 2026. Reporting to the Assistant Vice President of Information Technology, the Help Desk Technician provides 1 st line technical support to faculty, staff, and students in the resolution of hardware and software problems through assistance via phone, email or onsite. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. Position Type: Full-time, Temporary, Non-exemot Required Education: BA/BS degree in Computer Science or related discipline preferred. Qualifications: 2+ years’ experience relevant to 1 st line/help desk support; Proven experience using and troubleshooting Microsoft Office suite applications (Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Teams, One Drive); Demonstrated experience managing Outlook within a network environment; Excellent people skills, ability to interact effectively with diverse groups of people; Strong verbal communication skills, ability to disseminate information in a clear, concise manner both in person and via telephone; Well-developed organizational skills; Demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects, prioritize, and work efficiently; Professional appearance and demeanor; Strong knowledge of Microsoft based operating systems with emphasis on Windows desktop technologies; Familiarity with Smart board configurations and set up; Solid understanding of PC hardware set-up and configuration and imaging computers; Ability and willingness to support and promote the Felician Franciscan core values and mission of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume and 2 professional references electronically to: the Director or via USPS to: Mr. Carlos Caldero, Director Information Technology Felician University 262 South Main Street Lodi, New Jersey 07644 Salary Range:  $26.00-33.00/hour About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Assistant Professor, Cybersecurity and Computer Sciences Assistant Professor, Management and Entrepreneurial Studies Assistant Professor, Marketing Assistant Professor, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Sports Information Director and Intramurals Coordinator Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant/Associate Professor, Mathematics Associate Director for Academic Operations Associate Director of Housing Operations Associate Director of Student Accounts Associate Director of Student Financial Services Operations Associate Director of Transfer Student Success Associate Professor – PsyD Counseling Psychology Program Attitude Against Violence Project Coordinator Building and Grounds Assistant Campus Security: Part-time Security Officer Clinical Adjunct Faculty, Hybrid ABSN, Parsippany, School of Nursing Clinical Adjunct Faculty, School of Nursing, Traditional ABSN, Rutherfod NJ Director of Institutional Assessment and Accreditation Director of Internships and Assessment, School of Education Engagement and Philanth