 Careers at Felician Director of Institutional Assessment and Accreditation Felician University is presently seeking a focused, detail-oriented and analytically minded professional to serve as the Director of Institutional Assessment & Accreditation in the Center for Academic Success and Effectiveness.  The Director oversees the composition and coordination of assessment of student learning outcomes, assists in the evaluation of academic programs across departments and schools, integrates assessment activities and results with the MSCHE accreditation process, disseminates reported information to key University constituents and stakeholders and delivers training on assessment process, platforms and technologies across the University. Position Type: Full-time, 12-months, Exempt Department: Center for Academic Success and Effectiveness Date Posted: December 9, 2021 Required Education: Master’s Degree in higher education, education, sociology, psychology, statistics, research, program evaluation public administration or other related field required; extensive equivalent experience may be considered Qualifications: Minimum 3 years’ experience coordinating or overseeing outcomes assessment in a higher education setting; ability to learn and utilize assessment-related software for data collection, (Watermark, Qualtrics), data visualization and data analysis; proven experience supporting programmatic and/or regional accreditation processes; demonstrated familiarity with regional accreditation expectations (Middle states Commission on Higher Education preferred); proven experience in assessment support and training for faculty and staff; ability to work with data of varying levels of quality and validity; proven competence in managing multiple tasks and setting priorities; high degree of accuracy and attention to detail; demonstrated ability to work effectively in a collaborative environment; ability to foster and promote strong relationships with both internal and external stakeholders; willingness and ability to support and promote the Felician Franciscan mission and values of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume and 3 professional references electronically to: Dean or via USPS to: Dr. Jeffery Blanchard, Dean of the Center for Academic Success and Effectiveness Felician University 262 South Main Street Lodi, New Jersey 07644 Salary: Commensurate with experience About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Assistant Professor, Cybersecurity and Computer Sciences Assistant Professor, Management and Entrepreneurial Studies Assistant Professor, Marketing Assistant Professor, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Sports Information Director and Intramurals Coordinator Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant/Associate Professor, Mathematics Associate Director for Academic Operations Associate Director of Housing Operations Associate Director of Student Accounts Associate Director of Student Financial Services Operations Associate Director of Transfer Student Success Associate Professor – PsyD Counseling Psychology Program Attitude Against Violence Project Coordinator Building and Grounds Assistant Campus Security: Part-time Security Officer Clinica