ician Full-time Faculty, Prelicensure Nursing Felician University is currently seeking experienced, dedicated and academically qualified nursing specialist to teach in the School of Nursing.  Candidates should have experience teaching in both a traditional and online venues and must be willing to successfully complete Felician online certification.  S/he must have an educational background in the fundamentals of the discipline, as well as a wealth of real-world experience to bring to class discussions and case analyses. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. We offer a  choice of medical, dental, vision, and life insurance benefits, as well as a retirement plan (403B), tuition remission, and generous time off benefits. Position Type: Full-Time, 10-Month, Exempt Department: School of Nursing, Prelicensure Nursing Date Posted: March 20, 2024 Required Education: Master of Science in Nursing required, doctoral degree or progression towards such preferred Qualifications: Current licensure in good standing in New Jersey as a Registered Nurse. Current national certification in good standing. Current NJ Board of Nursing licensure in good standing as a Family Nurse Practitioner. Demonstrated knowledge and expertise in clinical nursing education. 2+ years’ practical experience in the area of specialization. Previous teaching experience, preferably in an institution of higher education. Superior written and verbal communications skills. Ability to engage with students of diverse backgrounds and experiences. Willingness and ability to support and promote the Felician Franciscan mission and values of the University. To Apply: Send CV and three (3) professional references to Associate Dean or via USPS to: Dr. Patricia Munno, Associate Dean School of Nursing Felician University 262 South Main S