Felician Evening and Weekend Circulation Supervisor Felician University, the Franciscan University of New Jersey, is offering an exciting opportunity for an outgoing, detail-oriented and student-centric professional to serve as the Evening and Weekend Circulation Supervisor for University Libraries on our Rutherford campus. The position is a part-time, flex position based upon the Felician University academic calendar. The Manager serves as the primary point of contact for all Library patrons at the Rutherford Campus Library. Position Type: Part-time, 10-month, Non-exempt Department: University Libraries Date Posted: Monday, March 27, 2023 Required Education: Bachelor’s degree required Qualifications: Superior organizational skills; strong time management skills; ability to manage multiple tasks simultaneously; good working knowledge of Microsoft Office applications (Word, Excel, Outlook); demonstrated ability to work effectively in a collaborative environment; ability and willingness to support and promote the Felician Franciscan mission and values of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume, and the names and contact information for (two) 2 professional references electronically to the Director or via USPS to: Ms. Jodi Shelly, Director University Libraries Felician University 262 South Main Street Lodi, New Jersey 07644 About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Maste