 Research and Instruction Librarian Felician University, the Franciscan University of New Jersey, is offering an exciting opportunity for an outgoing, detail-oriented, and student-centric professional to serve as the temporary Research and Instruction Librarian for the University Library.  The Research and Instruction Librarian supports a collegial environment with the central goals of service, instruction, and outreach. S/he supports the information-seeking, learning, and knowledge needs of Felician University, and is responsible for the collection and analysis of reference and operations data for Felician University Libraries. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. Position Type: Full-time, Temporary, Exempt Department: University Libraries Required Education: ALA-accredited Master’s degree in library and/or information science preferred, second Master’s degree preferred Qualifications: Thorough understanding of the structure and content of information resources in various formats;  teaching experience and strong presentation skills, preferably in a university setting; physical ability to lift boxes weighing up to 25 pounds; demonstrated reference and research skills in face-to-face and online formats; demonstrated teaching abilities, in both formal and informal venues; strong organizational skills; sound working knowledge of Microsoft Word, Excel, and e-mail applications; demonstrated ability to work effectively in a collaborative environment; familiarity with web-based social-media tools; well-developed interpersonal skills complemented by a predisposition to assist others; ability and willingness to work weekend and evening hours as needed to provide instruction; and/or reference services; willingness to support and uphold the University’s Catholic/Franciscan tradition and mission. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume, and the names and contact information for (two) 2 professional references electronically to the Director of Library Services or via USPS to: Ms. Jodi Shelly, Director University Libraries Felician University 262 South Main Street Lodi, New Jersey 07644 About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Assistant Professor, Cybersecurity and Computer Sciences Assistant Professor, Management and Entrepreneurial Studies Assistant Professor, Marketing Assistant Professor, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Sports Information Director and Intramurals Coordinator Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant/Associate Professor, Mathematics Associate Director for Academic Operations Associate Director of Housing Operations Associate Director of Student Accounts Associate Director of Student Financial Services Operations Associate Director of Transfer Student Success Associate Professor – PsyD Counseling Psychology Program Attitude Against Violence Project Coordinator Building and Grounds Assistant Campus Security: Part-time Security Officer Clinical Adjunct Faculty, Hybrid ABSN, Parsippany, School of Nursing Clinical Adjunct Faculty, School of Nursing, Traditi