lty Adjunct – Mathematics Felician University is offering exciting opportunities for Adjunct Professors in Mathematics for the 2026-2027 academic year (Fall 2026 and Spring 2027 semesters). Under the mentorship of full-time faculty, adjunct instructors will provide classroom experiences grounded in “best practices” for higher education and their respective disciplines. Position Type: Part-time, 1-2 courses per semester during the 2026-2027 academic year, maximum 3 days per week.  Day and evening classes available. Online and traditionsl classroom formates available. Department: School of Arts and Sciences, Mathematics Department Required Education: Master’s degree in Mathematics or closely related field required, Doctoral degree preferred. Qualifications: Experience teaching at the baccalaureate or graduate level reequired; evidence of onine teaching experience; ability and willingness to support the Felician Franciscan mission and values of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, current curriculum vitae, and the names of two professional references electronically to Interim Associate Dean or via USPS to: Dr. Gaby Fahmy School of Arts & Sciences Felician University 262 South Main Street Lodi, New Jersey  07644 Salary: Commensurate with rank and experience. Start Date: Review of candidate materials will begin effective immediately. About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, M