\\ Careers at Felician Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Felician University is presently offering an exciting opportunity for an energetic and goal-oriented individual with coaching experience in collegiate women’s basketball to serve as the Assistant Coach and Equipment Manager for our dynamic women’s basketball team.  The Assistant Coach serves as a primary instructor for players, as well as assisting the Head Coach in the supervision all aspects of a NCAA national Collegiate Women’s Basketball program.  Reporting to the Director of Athletics, the Assistant Coach assists in the preparation and execution of individual and team practices, training and competition; making travel arrangements for away competitions; identifying and recruiting potential women’s basketball student-athletes, including email, phone and mail correspondence; monitoring players’ academic progress; complying with all aspects of the Felician University Coach’s manual. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. We offer a choice of medical, dental, vision, and life insurance benefits, as well as a retirement plan (403B), tuition remission, and generous time off benefits. Required Education: Bachelor’s degree in related field required; may be waived for extensive practical experience in the field Qualifications: 2+ years’ successful basketball coaching experience; comprehensive knowledge of NCAA rules and regulations; ability to work well with a diverse group of student athletes; strong written and verbal communications skills; well-developed leadership skills; outstanding organizational and follow through skills; strong commitment to support and promote the Franciscan Felician values and function effectively within a Catholic University environment. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume and contact information for at least 3 professional references electronically to: Athletics Director or via USPS to: Mr. Andrew Toriello, Interim Director of Athletics Felician University 1 Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 Salary: Commensurate with experience About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer Assistant Director of Enrollment Management Services Assistant Director of Undergraduate Admissions Assistant Director, Center for Career and Professional Development Assistant Professor and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, Master’s Occupational Therapy Program Assistant Professor, Cybersecurity and Computer Sciences Assistant Professor, Management and Entrepreneurial Studies Assistant Professor, Marketing Assistant Professor, Prelicensure Nursing Assistant Sports Information Director and Intramurals Coordinator Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach and Equipment Manager Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Chemistry Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Sports Science Assistant/Associate Professor, Mathematics Associate Director for Academic Operations Associate Director of Housing Operations Associate Director of Student Accounts Associate Director of Student Financial Services Operations Associate Director of Transfer Student Success Associate Professor – PsyD Counseling Psychology Program Attitude Against Violence Project Coordinator Building and Grounds Assistant Campus Security: Part-time Security Officer Clinical Adjunct Faculty, Hybrid ABSN, Parsippany, School of Nursing Clinical Adjunct Faculty, School of Nursing, Traditional ABSN, Rutherfod NJ Director 