aculty, English Felician University is offering exciting opportunities for Adjunct Faculty in the English division of the School of Arts and Sciences for the 2026-2027 academic year. Under the mentorship of full-time faculty, adjunct faculty provide classroom experiences grounded in “best practices” for higher education and their respective disciplines. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. Position Type: Part-time, 1-2 courses per semester, maximum 3 days per week. Day and evening classes, online and traditional formats available. Department: School of Arts & Sciences, English Division Required Education: Master’s degree in English required, Doctoral degree preferred Qualifications: 1+ years’ teaching teaching experience at the baccalaureate level Proven experience of online teaching experence. Demonstrated familiarity with online teching platforms. Ability to engage effectively with a diverse student population. Willingness and ability to support and promote the Felician Franciscan core values and mission of the University To Apply: Send cover letter, current curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information for two professional references electronically to the Associate Dean of Humanities or via USPS to: Dr. Lavina Sequeira, Associate Dean of Humanities School of Arts & Sciences Felician University 262 South Main Street Lodi, New Jersey 07644 Salary: $700-800 per course credit About Felician University Accreditations Public Disclosure of Student Achievement Alumni Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Information Literacy Adjunct Faculty, Religious Studies Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services Assessment Data Coordinator Assistant Coach, Men’s Soccer Assistant Coach